A caller writes text before its {{template}} call, so the browser opens
<body> before the define runs and the define's own <body> is a misplaced
tag. The ancestors of the define's elements are then unknown, and the rule
main p might match p. It sets nowrap, which collapses whitespace exactly
like the normal p would inherit, so the answer is the same whether it
matches or not, and the body is re-indented.
-- input.gohtml --
<style>main p { white-space: nowrap; }</style>
{{define "GET /x X()"}}r{{template "p" .}}{{end}}
{{define "p"}}
<body>
<main>
<p>x</p>
</main>
</body>
{{end}}
-- format.gohtml --
<style>main p { white-space: nowrap; }</style>
{{define "GET /x X()"}}r{{template "p" .}}{{end}}
{{define "p"}}
<body>
	<main>
		<p>x</p>
	</main>
</body>
{{end}}
